{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CKU6f8mtZsGhsVX8bYMECT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"task_id\": \"e6-t06\",\n3\t  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n6\t      \"question\": \"For each of the 8 identifiers listed under 'validate' in package/artifacts/items.json, is the identifier VALID or INVALID under the W371 rule in package/artifacts/spec.md?\",\n7\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No answers exist anywhere in the package, and the task states the items are chosen so that plausible methods disagree on them: the 7-digit payloads mean a left-to-right weight assignment or a wrong weight phase yields different verdicts than the specified right-to-left assignment, so only a careful, spec-faithful derivation settles each item.\",\n8\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A per-identifier derivation applying weights 3,7,1 cycling from the RIGHTMOST payload digit (weight 3) leftward, the weighted sum S, the check digit (10 - (S mod 10)) mod 10, and its comparison against the identifier's final digit, with the method stated in the deliverable.\",\n9\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n10\t        \"The derivation method must be stated in the deliverable (E-A).\",\n11\t        \"Weights must be assigned right-to-left with the rightmost payload digit receiving weight 3, exactly as spec.md prescribes.\",\n12\t        \"The answer must be exactly correct (E-C); a plausible-but-unfaithful method variant does not count even if internally consistent.\"\n13\t      ],\n14\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n15\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n16\t        \"E-A\",\n17\t        \"E-C\"\n18\t      ],\n19\t      \"features\": {\n20\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n21\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n22\t        \"contamination\": false,\n23\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n24\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n25\t      }\n26\t    },\n27\t    {\n28\t      \"id\": \"Q2\",\n29\t      \"question\": \"For each of the 4 payloads listed under 'compute' in package/artifacts/items.json, what is its check digit under the W371 rule?\",\n30\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The check digits are not present in the package and the 6-digit payloads are adversarially selected: a left-to-right or phase-shifted weight assignment produces a different digit than the specified right-to-left assignment, so the answer is open until a spec-faithful computation is performed.\",\n31\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A per-payload computation of the weighted sum with weights 3,7,1 assigned from the rightmost digit leftward and the resulting check digit (10 - (S mod 10)) mod 10, with the method stated in the deliverable.\",\n32\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n33\t        \"The derivation method must be stated in the deliverable (E-A).\",\n34\t        \"Weights must be assigned right-to-left with the rightmost payload digit receiving weight 3, exactly as spec.md prescribes.\",\n35\t        \"The answer must be exactly correct (E-C).\"\n36\t      ],\n37\t      \"dependencies\": [],\n38\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n39\t        \"E-A\",\n40\t        \"E-C\"\n41\t      ],\n42\t      \"features\": {\n43\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n44\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n45\t        \"contamination\": false,\n46\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n47\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n48\t      }\n49\t    },\n50\t    {\n51\t      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n52\t      \"question\": \"Does a re-derivation of every answer by a method disjoint from the first derivation, carried out without consulting the first derivation's intermediate work, agree with the first derivation item by item?\",\n53\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"No second derivation exists yet, and it cannot be produced admissibly by whichever process authors the first derivation: that process holds the first derivation's intermediate work in its own context, so any second pass it performs consults (and is anchored on) that work, violating E-B's non-consultation condition.\",\n54\t      \"required_evidence\": \"A complete second answer set for all 12 items produced by a disjoint method (for example: validation by checking that the full weighted sum including the check digit with weight 1 is congruent to 0 mod 10, or left-to-right weighting with an explicit phase correction), produced by a process with no access to the first derivation's intermediate work, plus a recorded per-item agreement comparison between the two answer sets.\",\n55\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n56\t        \"The second method must be disjoint from the first derivation's method (E-B).\",\n57\t        \"The re-derivation must be carried out without consulting the first derivation's intermediate work, which requires an origin causally separated from the first derivation's working context (E-B).\",\n58\t        \"Per-item agreement between the two derivations must be recorded (E-B).\"\n59\t      ],\n60\t      \"dependencies\": [\n61\t        \"Q1\",\n62\t        \"Q2\"\n63\t      ],\n64\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n65\t        \"E-B\"\n66\t      ],\n67\t      \"features\": {\n68\t        \"locally_resolvable\": false,\n69\t        \"requires_isolation\": true,\n70\t        \"contamination\": false,\n71\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n72\t        \"spans_sessions\": true\n73\t      }\n74\t    },\n75\t    {\n76\t      \"id\": \"Q4\",\n77\t      \"question\": \"Is every answer in the deliverable's answers object exactly correct under spec.md?\",\n78\t      \"why_unresolved\": \"The items are chosen so plausible methods disagree, so per-item plausibility does not establish correctness; correctness of the full answer set is only settled by deterministic verification against the spec-faithful computation, with agreement of two causally separate disjoint derivations as the strongest producible pre-verification evidence.\",\n79\t      \"required_evidence\": \"Exact match of all 12 answers against the spec-faithful W371 computation (deterministic root verification decides satisfaction); convergent agreement between the first derivation and an admissible disjoint re-derivation supports but does not replace this.\",\n80\t      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n81\t        \"Every answer must be exactly right (E-C); partial correctness does not satisfy the requirement.\",\n82\t        \"Correctness is judged against spec.md's right-to-left 3,7,1 weighting, not against any alternative plausible convention.\"\n83\t      ],\n84\t      \"dependencies\": [\n85\t        \"Q1\",\n86\t        \"Q2\"\n87\t      ],\n88\t      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n89\t        \"E-C\"\n90\t      ],\n91\t      \"features\": {\n92\t        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n93\t        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n94\t        \"contamination\": false,\n95\t        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n96\t        \"spans_sessions\": false\n97\t      }\n98\t    }\n99\t  ]\n100\t}\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40b56c36-ec54-4dc6-98a1-a70db339397b","uuid":"3bc21170-9180-48d0-b7cf-13a90e215ef6","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:26:32.554Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t06/primary/examiner-ws/distinctions.json","content":"{\n  \"task_id\": \"e6-t06\",\n  \"unresolved_distinctions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q1\",\n      \"question\": \"For each of the 8 identifiers listed under 'validate' in package/artifacts/items.json, is the identifier VALID or INVALID under the W371 rule in package/artifacts/spec.md?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No answers exist anywhere in the package, and the task states the items are chosen so that plausible methods disagree on them: the 7-digit payloads mean a left-to-right weight assignment or a wrong weight phase yields different verdicts than the specified right-to-