eliverable (E-A).\",\n        \"Weights must be assigned right-to-left with the rightmost payload digit receiving weight 3, exactly as spec.md prescribes.\",\n        \"The answer must be exactly correct (E-C).\"\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [],\n      \"evidence_requirement_refs\": [\n        \"E-A\",\n        \"E-C\"\n      ],\n      \"features\": {\n        \"locally_resolvable\": true,\n        \"requires_isolation\": false,\n        \"contamination\": false,\n        \"capability_bearing_artifact\": false,\n        \"spans_sessions\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Q3\",\n      \"question\": \"Does a re-derivation of every answer by a method disjoint from the first derivation, carried out without consulting the first derivation's intermediate work, agree with the first derivation item by item?\",\n      \"why_unresolved\": \"No second derivation exists yet, and it cannot be produced admissibly by whichever process authors the first derivation: that process holds the first derivation's intermediate work in its own context, so any second pass it performs consults (and is anchored on) that work, violating E-B's non-consultation condition.\",\n      \"required_evidence\": \"A complete second answer set for all 12 items produced by a disjoint method (for example: validation by checking that the full weighted sum including the check digit with weight 1 is congruent to 0 mod 10, or left-to-right weighting with an explicit phase correction), produced by a process with no access to the first derivation's intermediate work, plus a recorded per-item agreement comparison between the two answer sets.\",\n      \"admissibility_constraints\": [\n        \"The second method must be disjoint from the first derivation's method (E-B).\",\n        \"The re-derivation must be carried out without consulting the first derivation's intermediate work, which requires an origin causally separated from the first derivation's working context (E-B).\",\n        \"Per-i