{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011fve71mmMF8LzjTFUu8xj1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Examiner charge — e6-t06 (node verify-independent)\n2\t\n3\tYou are the independent, information-only examiner for task e6-t06. You\n4\tre-verify; you do not write into the governed boundary and you have no\n5\tpromotion authority. Your product is a re-derivation report satisfying\n6\tevidence requirement E-B: a complete second answer set for all 12 items,\n7\tproduced by a method disjoint from the first derivation, without consulting\n8\tthe first derivation's intermediate work, with per-item agreement recorded.\n9\t\n10\t## Non-consultation condition (read this first)\n11\t\n12\t- You MUST NOT read `derivations.md` — it is the first derivation's\n13\t  intermediate work; reading it voids E-B.\n14\t- Derive your own answers for all 12 items FIRST, from\n15\t  `package/artifacts/spec.md` and `package/artifacts/items.json` only.\n16\t  Only after your 12 answers are fixed, open `result.json` and read its\n17\t  `answers` object (nothing else) to record the per-item comparison.\n18\t\n19\t## What to re-derive\n20\t\n21\tAll 12 items in `package/artifacts/items.json`:\n22\t- 8 identifiers under `validate` -> VALID or INVALID each.\n23\t- 4 payloads under `compute` -> one check digit each.\n24\t\n25\t## Required method (disjoint from the first derivation)\n26\t\n27\tThe first derivation tabulated digit-by-digit products walking the payload\n28\twith weights assigned right-to-left and then applied the check-digit\n29\tformula. Use a different route:\n30\t\n31\t1. For each `validate` identifier of length 8: treat the FINAL digit as\n32\t   position 0 and the payload digits as positions 1..7 counted from the\n33\t   right. Assign weight 1 to position 0 and weight 3,7,1,3,7,1,3 to\n34\t   positions 1..7 respectively (this is exactly spec.md's rule plus the\n35\t   check digit at weight 1). Compute the total T over ALL 8 digits.\n36\t   The identifier is VALID iff T mod 10 == 0. Do not compute the check\n37\t   digit explicitly.\n38\t2. For each `compute` payload of length 6: work LEFT to RIGHT with an\n39\t   explicit phase correction: the digit at left-to-right index i\n40\t   (i = 1..6) sits at right-to-left position p = 7 - i; its weight is 3 if\n41\t   p mod 3 == 1, 7 if p mod 3 == 2, 1 if p mod 3 == 0. Sum S, then the\n42\t   check digit is (10 - (S mod 10)) mod 10.\n43\t\n44\tCritical spec point to honor and to attack in the first derivation: spec.md\n45\tassigns weights RIGHT to LEFT with the RIGHTMOST payload digit at weight 3.\n46\tThe items are adversarially chosen so that a left-to-right assignment\n47\twithout phase correction, or any phase shift (rightmost = 7 or = 1), flips\n48\tverdicts and digits. If your total for any item differs, recompute that\n49\titem once from scratch before recording disagreement.\n50\t\n51\t## Answer components whose failure changes the deliverable\n52\t\n53\tEvery one of the 12 answers is load-bearing (E-C demands exact\n54\tcorrectness), but scrutinize hardest:\n55\t- The three INVALID verdicts claimed by the first derivation:\n56\t  `92489881`, `52874804`, `29067655`. A phase error typically turns\n57\t  exactly these.\n58\t- Every `compute` digit: `479812`, `153886`, `278381`, `027899`.\n59\t\n60\t## Report to produce\n61\t\n62\tFor each item: your independently derived answer, the `result.json`\n63\tanswer, and AGREE/DISAGREE. Then an overall verdict: whether the second\n64\tderivation agrees item by item (settles Q3) and whether any answer in\n65\t`result.json` is contradicted. Include your weighted totals so your work\n66\tis itself checkable.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"40b56c36-ec54-4dc6-98a1-a70db339397b","uuid":"ea5ad861-0e6f-4ce2-8f98-ca967ea6b04f","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:26:33.322Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t06/primary/examiner-ws/examiner-charge.md","content":"# Examiner charge — e6-t06 (node verify-independent)\n\nYou are the independent, information-only examiner for task e6-t06. You\nre-verify; you do not write into the governed boundary and you have no\npromotion authority. Your product is a re-derivation report satisfying\nevidence requirement E-B: a complete second answer set for all 12 items,\nproduced by a method disjoint from the first derivation, without consulting\nthe first derivation's intermediate work, with per-item agreement recorded.\n\n## Non-consultation condition (read this first)\n\n- You MUST NOT read `derivations.md` — it is the first derivation's\n  intermediate work; reading it voids E-B.\n- Derive your own answers for all 12 items FIRST, from\n  `package/artifacts/spec.md` and `package/artifacts/items.json` only.\n  Only after your 12 answers are fixed, open `result.json` and read its\n  `answers` object (nothing else) to record the per-item comparison.\n\n## What to re-derive\n\nAll 12 items in `package/artifacts/items.json`:\n- 8 identifiers under `validate` -> VALID or INVALID each.\n- 4 payloads under `compute` -> one check digit each.\n\n## Required method (disjoint from the first derivation)\n\nThe first derivation tabulated digit-by-digit products walking the payload\nwith weights assigned right-to-left and then applied the check-digit\nformula. Use a different route:\n\n1. For each `validate` identifier of length 8: treat the FINAL digit as\n   position 0 and the payload digits as positions 1..7 counted from the\n   right. Assign weight 1 to position 0 and weight 3,7,1,3,7,1,3 to\n   positions 1..7 respectively (this is exactly spec.md's rule plus the\n   check digit at weight 1). Compute the total T over ALL 8 digits.\n   The identifier is VALID iff T mod 10 == 0. Do not compute the check\n   digit explicitly.\n2. For each `compute` payload of length 6: work LEFT to RIGHT with an\n   explicit phase correction: the digit at left-to-right index i\n   (i = 1..6) sits at right-to-left position p = 7 - i; its weight is 3 if\n   p mod 3 == 1, 7 if p mod 3 == 2, 1 if p mod 3 == 0. Sum S, then the\n   check digit is (10 - (S mod 10)) mod 10.\n\nCritical spec point to honor and to attack in the first derivation: spec.md\nassigns weights RIGHT to LEFT with the RIGHTMOST payload digit at weight 3.\nThe items are adversarially chosen so that a left-to-right assignment\nwithout phase correction, or any phase shift (rightmost = 7 or = 1), flips\nverdicts and digits. If your total for any item differs, recompute that\nitem once from scratch before recording disagreement.\n\n## Answer components whose failure changes the deliverable\n\nEvery one of the 12 answers is load-bearing (E-C demands exact\ncorrectness), but scrutinize hardest:\n- The three INVALID verdicts claimed by the first derivation:\n  `92489881`, `52874804`, `29067655`. A phase error typically turns\n  exactly these.\n- Every `compute` digit: `479812`, `153886`, `278381`, `027899`.\n\n## Report to produce\n\nFor each item: your independently derived answer, the `result.json`\nanswer, and AGREE/DISAGREE. Then an overall verdict: whether the second\nderivation agrees item by item (settles Q3) and whether any answer in\n`result.json` is contradicted. Include your weighted totals so your work\nis itself checkable.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}}}
